 "components": {
  "schemas": {
   "AppSettings": {
    "properties": {
     "active_city_id": {
      "anyOf": [
       {
        "type": "integer"
       },
       {
        "type": "null"
       }
      ],
      "title": "Active City Id",
      "description": "null until the first city is added"
     },
     "description_language": {
      "type": "string",
      "minLength": 1,
      "title": "Description Language",
      "description": "Language Claude writes titles and descriptions in",
      "default": "русский"
     },
     "recent_posts": {
      "type": "integer",
      "maximum": 300.0,
      "minimum": 1.0,
      "title": "Recent Posts",
      "description": "How many latest posts of every channel are read; raising it reads older posts on the next refresh",
      "default": 20
     },
     "extraction_prompt": {
      "type": "string",
      "minLength": 1,
      "title": "Extraction Prompt",
      "description": "Instructions Claude gets for reading posts. Placeholders: {city}, {language}, {tags}, {fallback}",
      "default": "You turn Telegram channel posts into event cards for a person who lives in {city} and looks for things to do in person.\n\nFor every post return the events and places it announces. Most posts announce nothing: return empty lists for them.\n\nWhat to keep\n- Offline events that take place in {city}. Drop online events, events in other cities, ads, giveaways, news and reports about events that already happened.\n- A digest post that lists many events becomes one item per event.\n- A place with no date goes to \"places\", never to \"events\".\n\nThe description language is {language}. Allowed tags: {tags}. If none fits, use exactly \"{fallback}\".\nEach field's meaning is in the schema."
     },
     "matching_prompt": {
      "type": "string",
      "minLength": 1,
      "title": "Matching Prompt",
      "description": "Instructions Claude gets for merging duplicates",
      "default": "You merge duplicate event announcements collected from several Telegram channels.\n\nYou get existing event cards and new announcements. For every new announcement decide whether it describes the same real-world event as one of the existing cards, as one of the earlier new announcements, or neither.\n\nSame event: the same happening at the same place on the same date, even when titles differ or are in different languages. Also the same: a post that reschedules, cancels or adds details to an event announced earlier (update_kind says so), and a single date of a recurring event that has a recurring card.\nNot the same: different events at the same venue on the same day; the same show or tour on different dates; different sessions of a festival when each is its own event.\n\nNever set both same_as_card and same_as_announcement."
     }
    },
    "type": "object",
    "required": [
     "active_city_id",
     "description_language",
     "recent_posts",
     "extraction_prompt",
     "matching_prompt"
    ],
    "title": "AppSettings",
    "description": "Every setting of the app, described once: storage, the API and its change request all come from here."
   },
